- [will_said] PHCC RULINGS — ARTIFACTS, BINARY, HASHMAP, CONFORMANCE: (a) Build artifacts: generated assembly VISIBLE and PERSISTENT with environment + compiler versions recorded; ALL text and binary artifacts stay in the phext (binaries base64, xz seal over the ENTIRE phext as publish form, working phext plain); artifacts at Library 10000, wiped/reset often. Outcome: assembly is objdump disassembly with full provenance; binary scrolls converted to the canonical PR #9 format, bit-identical, interop proven. (b) BINARY-INGESTION RULE (verbatim): 'when non-utf8 data is observed in an incoming scroll update, we encode it with base64 verbatim' — exactly as observed, no rejection/panic/normalisation, for the update path; canonical for all ports. (c) HASHMAP: 'phcc should use the hashmap interface to speedup compilation, don't worry about working directly on the buffer most of the time' — lookups via the coordinate->scroll hashmap, direct buffer work only load/save. F4 complete: random gets 108 -> 42 ns (2.5x), break-even ~23k lookups, insert honestly unchanged, conformance/fuzz clean. (d) CONFORMANCE: hard compatibility with gcc, clang, MSVC; MSVC is WILL'S MANUAL ACT ('I will confirm msvc compatibility manually when I merge') — his signed attestation at merge, never an automated run; Windows x86_64 a primary platform alongside Linux. Windows readiness: 14/14 cross-target compile + link receipts (PE verified, none executed). Conformance slice 1: 333 probes, gcc = clang 333/333, three-way 326/333; two silent defects (__attribute__((packed)) and ((aligned(N))) inert). F5 root cause CORRECTS the slice-1 guess — attributes were never parsed: glibc defines __attribute__ as an EMPTY macro for compilers declaring neither __GNUC__ nor __clang__, and tccpp expanded the keyword away. After fix: conformance 328/333, rest documented class (b).
- [observed] PHCC BENCHMARKS + WAVES + GATE v2 GREEN (final states): SQLite — phcc compiles sqlite3.c in 0.051 s vs gcc-O2 13.11 s (~250x), outputs byte-identical; self-host: phcc builds itself in 0.255 s, phcc-built phcc passes make test; runtime binaries 1.4-2.7x slower than -O2 oracles. Will's gate [will_said]: matrix expanded (sqlite, ffmpeg, libtool, gawk, sed, grep, coreutils, vim, openssl, zlib, Lua 5.4, git); phcc may not be published as a real competitor until it builds them; -O2 (today a no-op) is to become a real phext-powered mode; killer feature: auto-amalgamation for free. Fixes F6-F24 landed across Waves 1-6. Gate v1: NOT all-green. Gate v2 (published tip): GREEN — all 11 projects build from clean trees; sed/grep gnulib-tests pass, git 706/706, gawk+MPFR all passed, FFmpeg transcode byte-identical to gcc, OpenSSL subsets pass both configs with only the rsa_complex class-(b) error lines. Recon closed: libtool's 9 failures were F6/F10 link deaths; gawk's 6 failures reproduce under gcc-built gawk on aletheia-core (no libmpfr headers) — caveat: gawk make check there is not a compiler signal unless libmpfr-dev is present. Still open: PQ-22 (General-Dynamic TLS) and PQ-23 static.
