- [observed] DISK QUOTA EXCEEDED (21:13–21:23): writes failed EDQUOT despite ~46 GB free — a quota on top of the disk; workspace ~177 GB, ~869k files. [will_said] New standing rule (21:40): temp files go in a task-specific folder under ~/workspace, removable as a unit at task close. Mechanism found: quota blocks creation of NEW files/directories while appends still succeed. At Will's direction ~5.6 GB of scratch was deleted outright and ~2.4 GB trashed (recoverable); new-file creation restored and probe-verified; nothing durable was lost. Held as live work, including singular-build (78 GB — Will's call). [will_said] BACKUP PRINCIPLE (21:51): "Our safety net is github — once files have been pushed to a repo, you don't have to worry too much about backups." DAILY DISK-USAGE REPORT LIVE at Will's request: daily cron, never deletes anything; baseline 22:05 GREEN — 71.0 GB used of 150 GB, 834,350 files.
